{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>who have sharpened</b> — like a sharpened arrow." "<b>to aim their arrow</b> — I already explained it in the verse \"he prepares his arrows\" [Psalm 64:7?], for the meaning is: they aim their bow with arrows. Some say: for a bitter thing has come upon their tongue or this deed of theirs."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 64, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:38.834107627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}